{
  "summary": "The supplied methods show a path from repository readiness through FastCode.query, retrieval, answer generation, and optional session storage. They establish static boundaries, not that the read-only sample ran or that any answer succeeded.",
  "conclusions": [
    {
      "dimension_id": "query_flow",
      "text": "The MCP code_qa caller first requests ready repository names, then loads their indexes, and returns an error string if either step fails. It passes those names as repo_filter to FastCode.query. FastCode.query separately requires repo_indexed to be true before entering its query try block. The readiness and loading helpers themselves were not supplied.",
      "source_ids": ["3bdeac89956f17801807b9abaeba7a998c39e5ab56d7a6549998c3e2c916f566", "3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "query_flow",
      "text": "FastCode.query selects its preprocessing branch from retriever.enable_agency_mode AND the presence of retriever.iterative_agent. That branch constructs a minimal ProcessedQuery and skips query_processor.process; otherwise it calls process with dialogue history and use_llm_enhancement=True. It passes use_agency_mode onward to retriever.retrieve, but that argument does not control this earlier branch.",
      "source_ids": ["3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "query_flow",
      "text": "The standard query-processing implementation was not supplied. The provided enhancement helper selects OpenAI or Anthropic, returns an empty dictionary for other providers or caught errors, and parses a response when available; this does not establish when process invokes it.",
      "source_ids": ["3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c", "f2622f98a09110fdfebee5dbfd2a829116714e44a8ff2597765ee849511d6c64"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "query_flow",
      "text": "FastCode.query sends the ProcessedQuery, filters, repo_filter, agency override, and—when multi-turn is enabled—summary history to retriever.retrieve. Supplied retrieval helpers show semantic search passing repo_filter into the vector store and checking returned repository names again; separate helpers filter language, type, and relative file path, and remove results outside the requested repositories. Without retrieve's body, their invocation and ordering on this path remain unverified.",
      "source_ids": ["3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c", "c4c8a1aae4e8162a15519af3e047c6c6950e9881997bcb98432ee4e2f3aeaa66", "42e32ad5d9ffdb60e15ef62b7fcc5804da659c2f14129552fead458bfdec396e", "ff351f4dfda0da31e1e6f6f083b5adb3680d261d105c6e41f7abf63a8caa8648"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "query_flow",
      "text": "The supplied agency helper reconstructs a ProcessedQuery and calls iterative_agent.retrieve_with_iteration when an agent exists. It returns the original results if the agent is absent or the helper catches an exception. Whether retriever.retrieve calls this helper for the sample is unknown.",
      "source_ids": ["e7510cca5235adc213f163d7d6130ce424c3c74615346a2a807d73fcddc3627c"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "query_flow",
      "text": "After retrieval, FastCode.query calls AnswerGenerator.generate with the original question, retrieved elements, processed-query metadata, full dialogue history from a separate helper, and an optional prompt builder. generate prepares context, builds a prompt, selects a provider, and returns answer and source metadata; the context-preparation, prompt-building, and source-extraction bodies were not supplied.",
      "source_ids": ["3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c", "958b22f075bddc6f043298013789b6356f21e03c874dc11881f51cd6b74b6b4d"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "state_ownership",
      "text": "code_qa owns the tool-call session identifier: it uses the supplied session_id or creates a short UUID-derived one, passes it to FastCode.query, and appends it to returned text. FastCode.query obtains recent summaries only when multi-turn is enabled and a session ID is present; its configured history_summary_rounds defaults to 10.",
      "source_ids": ["3bdeac89956f17801807b9abaeba7a998c39e5ab56d7a6549998c3e2c916f566", "3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "state_ownership",
      "text": "FastCode.query attempts to save a dialogue turn whenever session_id exists, including single-turn calls. It stores the answer, optional summary, JSON-serializable formatted sources, and metadata rather than the raw retrieved elements; it does not inspect save_dialogue_turn's Boolean return before logging that the turn was saved.",
      "source_ids": ["3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c", "18bd1442ebf14ca13388be94fcc2884400bbcbd9d893e24058b3934245f40f20"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "state_ownership",
      "text": "CacheManager.save_dialogue_turn returns false when cache storage is disabled or an exception is caught. When enabled, it constructs turn data, calls self.set, updates a session index, and returns true, but does not check self.set's result. Query-result cache reads and writes in FastCode.query are commented out, so they are not the active query path shown.",
      "source_ids": ["18bd1442ebf14ca13388be94fcc2884400bbcbd9d893e24058b3934245f40f20", "3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "state_ownership",
      "text": "The supplied persistence methods have distinct owners: VectorStore.save writes a FAISS index and pickled metadata unless in-memory mode skips saving; HybridRetriever.save_bm25 and CodeGraphBuilder.save write separate pickle files. The MCP _is_repo_indexed helper checks only for a named FAISS file and metadata pickle, so that check alone does not establish that other indexes are present or loadable.",
      "source_ids": ["0d0864e396269bcb455b2662e28f479a30dc0df72b55b79a038c4703d11862ec", "2a6b1d5e31cbaca965ffb0ed0009e8ba4bcb9d9091b0a2d7ce5912644e474bd9", "a8f62f0083e424b3040b89ae0b66c4ea0c393149f664bb4bfe141baa5fa4be7e", "ec940072e8ca2e7ae26e6b4d4b6f08d448095dc31cab91ba93a21f36f649ba64"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "failure_boundaries",
      "text": "The not-indexed check in FastCode.query raises RuntimeError outside its try block. Exceptions inside that block are instead converted to a result dictionary containing error text. AnswerGenerator.generate also returns an error dictionary for exceptions in its provider-call and response-handling try block.",
      "source_ids": ["3c55fe0f547e22c5019fbc6f09e537128205c4c3869ffd8eae3d0a204694f60c", "958b22f075bddc6f043298013789b6356f21e03c874dc11881f51cd6b74b6b4d"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "failure_boundaries",
      "text": "AnswerGenerator.generate prepares context, builds the prompt, and counts or truncates tokens before its provider-call try block; errors in those earlier operations are not caught by that block. Its preflight limit is max_context_tokens minus max_tokens minus reserve_tokens. After truncation it recounts the rebuilt prompt, but the shown method does not reject it if it still exceeds that limit.",
      "source_ids": ["958b22f075bddc6f043298013789b6356f21e03c874dc11881f51cd6b74b6b4d", "6e88811451cda06d0d7c8b87b79fde3880f897677a4c59d2e8b445cb70fabc30"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "failure_boundaries",
      "text": "An optional custom prompt builder is used to construct and reconstruct the actual prompt, while the truncation budget estimates base tokens using _build_prompt. The supplied code therefore does not prove that a custom-built final prompt fits the calculated budget.",
      "source_ids": ["958b22f075bddc6f043298013789b6356f21e03c874dc11881f51cd6b74b6b4d"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "failure_boundaries",
      "text": "Unconfigured providers and uninitialized clients can yield strings beginning with 'Error' rather than exceptions; generate can place such strings in an ordinary answer result. By contrast, the shown OpenAI and Anthropic non-streaming helpers raise on missing response content. The MCP caller reads answer and sources, not the result's error field, and appends a session ID, so returned text or a session ID alone does not prove successful generation.",
      "source_ids": ["958b22f075bddc6f043298013789b6356f21e03c874dc11881f51cd6b74b6b4d", "64e53597abdf83d3827430a880cb98d05ad1364d9d46aca28b995d8e140a279e", "7dbc6309168db0b0fdf528caeb2dd6ee65b604ae89d35cd3160bb3c9816f8c96", "3bdeac89956f17801807b9abaeba7a998c39e5ab56d7a6549998c3e2c916f566"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "scope_and_verification",
      "text": "For a local path, RepositoryLoader.load_from_path requires an existing directory. It reuses the path if it already equals the workspace destination; otherwise it prepares that destination and copies the entire working tree, including untracked files, with symlinks preserved. _prepare_repo_path calls a backup helper if the destination exists. Thus loading is not intrinsically read-only, and the backup helper's effects are not shown.",
      "source_ids": ["3ea8337a4cc79f1c2bcb7141801a9fd23b61a3ed19eae6baa193e997c63c4aad", "f30079af74f72d237599ee302df22093afc8fcfcef16cff1f5f54a8adeaf237a"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "scope_and_verification",
      "text": "The supplied parser entry routes Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, C/C++, Rust, and C# to language-specific methods, and other languages to a generic parser. Incremental indexing skips files whose content cannot be read or whose parse result is None. A separate syntax-fix method exists, but these bodies do not show whether it is called for the sample or what its parser accepted.",
      "source_ids": ["895930b6378e96bcc4e2cb5369b44aa1d53e9e2f363a2a55a2e8a0c877dee63b", "2dff45803c5c2609981a1dac4cbdcbf1f712a465199acef081018a2e3712cfde", "16f555bbef39f866b83fd033ea08bacc47b239785b29f138c159da80d03911a0"]
    },
    {
      "dimension_id": "scope_and_verification",
      "text": "Related entry boundaries are visible without exercising them: API and web load-and-index endpoints call load_repository followed by index_repository; the MCP reindex_repo tool forces indexing and then clears in-memory indexed/loaded state. These are navigation points, not evidence that a particular repository was indexed.",
